00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
When working with Word documents,
there may be occasions you wish to

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:07.800
password protect the document, so that
only yourself and and others who are

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.030
allowed access, can open the file.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.030
This may be because it contains
sensitive or personal information.

00:00:14.879 --> 00:00:19.220
To add protection to a document,
you first open the document and then

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.470
simply navigate up to the file menu.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.960
And from there select info, and once
you've selected info you will click

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.459
on the protect document button.

00:00:29.049 --> 00:00:32.520
This will give you a number of options
of how you can protect the document.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.860
The two we are going to
look at are encrypt with

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.660
password and restrict editing.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.800
So if I click on the encrypt with
password, it will then bring up the

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:47.220
password dialog box and I will create
the password, select OK, and again,

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:54.620
it will ask for this to be entered
twice just to ensure it's correct.

00:00:55.349 --> 00:00:55.989
Click OK.

00:00:56.129 --> 00:00:57.960
And that has now protected the document.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.140
That protection won't be applied
until I select save, so if I

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.059
saved it now, it will protect it.

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:06.960
But if I close the document and didn't
save it, it would still be unprotected.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:10.140
So I click save and
then close the document.

00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:16.130
The next time I go to open the
document, it will ask for a

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:23.360
password, enter the password, and
that will then open the document.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.440
If at a point in the future, I wish to
remove the password, I would quite simply

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:36.150
go to file, info, protect document,
encrypt with password, and then remove

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.310
the password, leave it blank, select OK.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:42.330
And as you can see, that
has now gone back to normal.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.860
Again, if I don't save that, the
password will still be active, so I

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.680
need to click save and close that now.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:54.975
And then when I open it again, it will
simply open without asking for a password.

00:01:55.035 --> 00:01:58.955
There may be occasions when, rather than
adding a password, you may just restrict

00:01:59.025 --> 00:02:02.655
the editing of the document so that people
can read it, but they can't make any

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:07.905
changes such as add more text or delete
information contained within the document.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:12.915
Again, to do this, you can add
protection so that the file is read only.

00:02:13.065 --> 00:02:19.185
So if you go to File and then
info and on the protect document

00:02:19.245 --> 00:02:21.525
dropdown, select restrict editing.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:26.235
And this will open up the restrict
editing dialogue box to the right.

00:02:27.315 --> 00:02:30.645
So what you're looking for in here is
to ensure that the editing restrictions

00:02:31.215 --> 00:02:34.605
are applied as "no changes read only".

00:02:35.175 --> 00:02:38.775
Later in the course, you will be required
to create some forms where you will need

00:02:38.775 --> 00:02:43.365
to select filling in forms, but in this
instance, to purely protect the document

00:02:43.365 --> 00:02:48.825
from any changes, I need to make sure that
no changes, read only is selected and then

00:02:48.825 --> 00:02:50.955
select yes, start enforcing protection.

00:02:51.915 --> 00:02:56.685
Now again, if I don't put a password in
here, then people will be able to go into

00:02:56.805 --> 00:02:58.605
the editing restrictions and make changes.

00:02:58.605 --> 00:03:06.205
So if I just add a password and
reenter to confirm, select OK,

00:03:08.025 --> 00:03:09.765
and then that is now protected.

00:03:09.795 --> 00:03:15.840
So if I close that and I try and
make any changes it won't allow me.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.720
It will give the box up
so there's a warning.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.410
So this document is protected from
unintentional editing, you may

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:28.380
only view this region and there
are no regions that can be edited.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:31.680
They could click on stop protection, but
they would need the password to be able

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.260
to make any changes to the document.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:38.430
And every time they type in,
they would make it try to make

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:41.120
a change, nothing will happen.

